{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/55","id":4687016182,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF14w9g","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/55","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/55.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/55.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/55","number":55,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Give a reviewed combinatorial Hurwitz polytope comparison","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Result\n\nA combinatorial proof of the projected discriminant/Hurwitz weight-polytope comparison requested by OWR-14299288-015, in the smooth, complete very ample, degree-at-least-two regime of the source's cited Sano theorem.\n\nThe argument combines a product-face centroid identity, finite-difference cancellation, equal-column regular refinements, and the established GKZ normal-fan compatibility. The support-function step proves the reverse inclusion without assuming that every projected discriminant vertex remains a vertex. The previously known geometric equality, GKZ foundations, Sano's analytic description, and Ogusu–Sano's surface inclusion are credited.\n\n## Scope\n\n- The complete proof is in `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/CANDIDATE.md`\n- Smoothness, complete lattice-point embeddings, and the source's degree hypothesis are retained\n- This is a combinatorial comparison within established GKZ theory, not a reconstruction of its foundations\n- Arbitrary singular or incomplete configurations are outside the claim\n- Historical novelty is unestablished\n\n## Independent validation\n\nA separate adversarial review passes the complete intended comparison and explicitly checks both the restored source hypotheses and requested proof type. The unchanged report and source-verification receipt are included under `review/`.\n\n- 1,227 author exact assertions, reproduced byte-for-byte\n- 8,093 independent exact lower-hull assertions, reproduced byte-for-byte\n- Frozen mathematical artifact SHA-256: `4931eccbb464b53af07b90e24b72060e681b9a7f1769c0030a9d7090e59b129c`\n\nThe finite checks are diagnostics alongside the general proof. This is separate AI review, not human peer review. Please keep this PR open as a draft for further examination.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T06:56:32Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:58:26Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2d86411e3b0560ce6bdcbc5c807e8f29b2208717","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/55/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/55/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/55/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/85c78d0cf3959d9d492a637cb90835ebc6a0e828","head":{"label":"Alec